  "findings": [
    "Generalisation gap: the deterministic engine stops 100.0% of attacks on the corpus it was developed against but 18.8% of the held-out set, at sub-millisecond latency (p95 0.71ms) and zero marginal cost. Rules are a regression floor, not a generalising detector.",
    "prompt-guard-86m alone reaches 72.5% held-out injection recall but 0.0% on harmful-content requests: it is an injection classifier, not a content-safety model.",
    "Cascade calls the classifier on 2% of requests and reaches 20.8% recall; running it on every request reaches 64.6%. The difference is the attacks that carry no lexical signal at all: the cascade cannot escalate what the rules never saw.",
    "OpenAI moderation catches 100.0% of held-out harmful requests and 0.0% of injections: moderation APIs do not cover prompt injection, so they cannot replace an injection layer.",
    "Best F1 on held-out data: Deterministic + prompt-guard-86m + safeguard-20b (0.970)."
  ],
